WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.033 --> 00:00:02.969 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:02.969 --> 00:00:04.370
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.574
Welcome back to Correctshuns
for the week of August 9th.

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:10.643
We missed you guys,

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.945
and we're looking forward
to getting right into it.

00:00:12.945 --> 00:00:15.381
I -- very strange for me,

00:00:15.381 --> 00:00:18.485
but I want to start off
by apologizing to Donald Trump

00:00:18.485 --> 00:00:21.154
for an error I made in
this week's Closer Look.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:25.891
We talked about how when
he was a USFL team owner,

00:00:25.891 --> 00:00:29.929
the USFL sued the NFL
for an antitrust violation,

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:33.032
and they sued
for $1.7 million --

00:00:33.032 --> 00:00:34.100
or a billion dollars.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.501
I guess it must have been
$1.7 billion.

00:00:35.501 --> 00:00:37.903
And they received a dollar.
They were awarded a dollar.

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:39.438
And we sort of made fun
of Donald Trump

00:00:39.438 --> 00:00:41.674
for the fact that
he was awarded a dollar.

00:00:41.674 --> 00:00:45.678
But I made a mistake
because in antitrust cases,

00:00:45.678 --> 00:00:47.747
damages are tripled.

00:00:47.747 --> 00:00:50.083
So in the end, they got $3.

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:58.457
So you are good at business.

00:00:58.457 --> 00:01:02.795
I referenced one of
my favorite shows, "Hot Ones,"

00:01:02.795 --> 00:01:04.697
where people eat hot,

00:01:04.697 --> 00:01:05.932
progressively hotter
chicken wings

00:01:05.932 --> 00:01:08.534
and said no one would do
that show twice.

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:09.602
Some people have done it twice.

00:01:09.602 --> 00:01:12.205
Steve-O has done it twice,
of course.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:13.606
Eric Andre has done it twice.

00:01:13.606 --> 00:01:16.075
So I apologize
that I got that wrong.

00:01:16.075 --> 00:01:18.444
I also said that as soon
as I did "Hot Ones,"

00:01:18.444 --> 00:01:22.415
the next interview I did was
with Terry Gross at "Fresh Air,"

00:01:22.415 --> 00:01:24.783
because I wanted to do
an interview

00:01:24.783 --> 00:01:27.553
where I wasn't worried
that I'd have to excuse myself

00:01:27.553 --> 00:01:30.289
because I was gonna
[bleep] my pants.

00:01:30.289 --> 00:01:31.824
And someone said,
"Hey, those are --

00:01:31.824 --> 00:01:33.359
you do Terry Gross
over the phone,

00:01:33.359 --> 00:01:37.096
so you wouldn't
have to excuse yourself."

00:01:37.096 --> 00:01:41.234
I think even if I was
on the phone with someone,

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:42.468
I wouldn't just like, [bleep].

00:01:42.468 --> 00:01:43.903
I wouldn't take advantage
of the fact

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:44.904
that we were on the phone
to be like,

00:01:44.904 --> 00:01:48.340
"I'm gonna [bleep] my pants."

00:01:48.340 --> 00:01:51.210
But it is true
that you do "Fresh Air,"

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:52.912
you do not
do "Fresh Air" in person

00:01:52.912 --> 00:01:56.516
unless you're
Seth [bleep] Meyers, pal.

00:01:59.018 --> 00:02:03.556
You guys should just
start doing apologies.

00:02:06.091 --> 00:02:08.094
Didn't want to hold up
an art card, guys,

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:10.396
'cause it's -- we talked
about my fingernails.

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:13.066
I don't even want to
hold up my hands.

00:02:13.066 --> 00:02:14.634
They're bad.

00:02:14.634 --> 00:02:16.635
You guys said I have terrible --

00:02:16.635 --> 00:02:20.106
I needed a manicure, and I tried
really hard over the hiatus

00:02:20.106 --> 00:02:22.508
to stop chewing my nails,
and it didn't go well.

00:02:22.508 --> 00:02:26.445
My goal is to
have really beautiful hands,

00:02:26.445 --> 00:02:28.548
should we ever hold up,

00:02:28.548 --> 00:02:30.850
as Shoemaker calls it,
Lady Emmy.

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:34.387
And...

00:02:34.387 --> 00:02:37.390
But the one thing
I'm not gonna do

00:02:37.390 --> 00:02:39.792
is what all my colleagues
in the late night field --

00:02:39.792 --> 00:02:44.296
I will not use a hand model.

00:02:44.296 --> 00:02:46.666
You think when Kimmel
holds up an album,

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.200
you think those are his hands?

00:02:48.200 --> 00:02:49.369
Grow up.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:03:01.280
We mentioned the song "Gasolina"
and said it was a Pitbull song.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.414
This was before the break,

00:03:02.414 --> 00:03:06.286
and it's just been
a relentless two weeks

00:03:06.286 --> 00:03:09.555
of people telling us
it's a Daddy Yankee song.

00:03:09.555 --> 00:03:11.323
My favorite phrasing of it was,

00:03:11.323 --> 00:03:18.230
"What gringo on your staff
thought it was Pitbull?"

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:20.500
Se llama Alex Baze.

00:03:23.502 --> 00:03:27.307
[ Speaking in Spanish ]

00:03:32.579 --> 00:03:37.717
Pitbull is on a remix
of "Gasolina."

00:03:37.717 --> 00:03:43.356
And Baize is always
about the remixes.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:47.360
When there's a new remix
of a popular song,

00:03:47.360 --> 00:03:49.629
we don't even expect
to see him in the office.

00:03:49.629 --> 00:03:53.532
He loves to take an original

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:55.434
and just remix it
and make it better,

00:03:55.434 --> 00:03:57.604
unless it's one of his jokes.

00:04:03.076 --> 00:04:05.945
We talked about Ronnie Jackson,
who was the president's doctor.

00:04:05.945 --> 00:04:09.114
Dr. Ronnie is now a congressman.

00:04:09.114 --> 00:04:12.551
And we put up a key
where he was playing a flute,

00:04:12.551 --> 00:04:15.488
and this is another one
where a lot of people got to us.

00:04:15.488 --> 00:04:17.590
He was holding
the flute to the left.

00:04:17.590 --> 00:04:20.292
Flutes only go to the right.

00:04:20.292 --> 00:04:21.794
I did not know that,

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:25.797
and I don't
want to know any more.

00:04:25.797 --> 00:04:29.369
I will take your word for it
and let's end it there.

00:04:33.171 --> 00:04:36.175
I can't believe we've got
to put up this graphic again.

00:04:36.175 --> 00:04:38.911
This is now a month ago.

00:04:38.911 --> 00:04:41.981
We put up a graphic of me

00:04:41.981 --> 00:04:43.983
getting a drive-through
appendectomy.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:45.351
Alex, can we put it up
real quick?

00:04:45.351 --> 00:04:48.688
And originally,
first thing we heard was,

00:04:48.688 --> 00:04:50.757
that's not where
the appendectomy scar was.

00:04:50.757 --> 00:04:53.025
The next thing we heard was,
you should be wearing a mask.

00:04:53.025 --> 00:04:55.327
Next thing we heard was,
you're driving the wrong way

00:04:55.327 --> 00:04:57.664
through the drive-through,
based on the arrow.

00:05:00.133 --> 00:05:04.304
And then finally someone said,
"Why do you have a guitar?"

00:05:08.641 --> 00:05:12.945
And like,
we've talked about this,

00:05:12.945 --> 00:05:20.085
that the graphics team,
they like to get in trouble.

00:05:20.085 --> 00:05:24.456
They're just like,
little stinkers.

00:05:24.456 --> 00:05:25.791
And I heard this
and I went down.

00:05:25.791 --> 00:05:28.060
I'm like, "Why did you guys
put a guitar in there?

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:29.695
You know, I don't play guitar,
right?"

00:05:29.695 --> 00:05:35.801
And they were like,
"Yeah, we know."

00:05:35.801 --> 00:05:38.371
I was like, "Also, did you know
flutes only go to the right?"

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:40.306
"Uh-huh."

00:05:45.844 --> 00:05:48.814
Talked about that if Trump --
this is based on the whole

00:05:48.814 --> 00:05:52.451
Four Seasons Hotel
and Four Seasons landscaping.

00:05:52.451 --> 00:05:55.621
We had a joke,
if Trump told Rudy

00:05:55.621 --> 00:05:58.324
to do something
at a Waldorf Astoria,

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:01.393
he would do it
at a Walmart in Astoria.

00:06:01.393 --> 00:06:04.597
There's no Walmart in Astoria.

00:06:04.597 --> 00:06:06.599
I wrote that joke. I checked.

00:06:06.599 --> 00:06:09.602
I saw, I knew
there was no Walmart in Astoria.

00:06:09.602 --> 00:06:11.003
Still told it.

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:20.579
Knitting.

00:06:20.579 --> 00:06:21.780
We talked about
a grandmother saying,

00:06:21.780 --> 00:06:23.483
"Hey, it's knitting time.

00:06:25.485 --> 00:06:26.952
Put down that 'Grand Theft Auto'

00:06:26.952 --> 00:06:28.420
and help me crochet
this blanket."

00:06:28.420 --> 00:06:34.893
Well, knitting and crocheting
are two very different things,

00:06:34.893 --> 00:06:36.895
I've been told.

00:06:36.895 --> 00:06:40.232
And I want to read a comment
someone had about it.

00:06:40.232 --> 00:06:42.134
I'm not going to
read the first sentence.

00:06:42.134 --> 00:06:43.669
I'm gonna go back and pick up
the first sentence.

00:06:43.669 --> 00:06:46.038
Someone wrote,

00:06:46.038 --> 00:06:49.775
"Knitting and crocheting
are completely different,

00:06:49.775 --> 00:06:52.444
and that lady is working
a sleeve or a sock.

00:06:52.444 --> 00:06:55.714
Definitely not an Afghan.
Definitely not crochet.

00:06:55.714 --> 00:06:58.417
Sloppy work, guys."

00:06:58.417 --> 00:07:02.021
The first sentence was,
"Are you [bleep] kidding me?"

00:07:05.524 --> 00:07:07.759
Definitely not lining up
with my stereotype

00:07:07.759 --> 00:07:09.762
of the knitting community.

00:07:12.164 --> 00:07:14.667
It's like, watching
A Closer Look.

00:07:14.667 --> 00:07:16.736
The [bleep]?

00:07:22.174 --> 00:07:25.044
Talked about somebody wearing

00:07:25.044 --> 00:07:27.646
one of the flying squirrel suits
cliff diving.

00:07:27.646 --> 00:07:31.950
I was told that
would be base diving.

00:07:31.950 --> 00:07:38.623
We talked about Jeff Bezos
jetting to space,

00:07:38.623 --> 00:07:40.425
jetting off to space.

00:07:40.425 --> 00:07:45.864
Someone said you don't jet
to space, you rocket to space.

00:07:45.864 --> 00:07:49.635
And you can [bleep] off
to space.

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:56.775
Oh, someone said that, hey,
that during a correction,

00:07:56.775 --> 00:07:59.511
sometimes I hold
my arm like this

00:07:59.511 --> 00:08:01.981
and it looks like
I'm going to dislocate it,

00:08:01.981 --> 00:08:05.518
and that is what
I'm trying to do.

00:08:08.821 --> 00:08:12.491
I'm trying to like put
the discomfort here

00:08:12.491 --> 00:08:15.261
to distract from this.

00:08:19.665 --> 00:08:25.571
So we have these
jackal mugs we've been making.

00:08:25.571 --> 00:08:27.506
These are not available
in the NBC store,

00:08:27.506 --> 00:08:30.376
because NBC hates money.

00:08:30.376 --> 00:08:33.011
And so this one, we put up,

00:08:33.011 --> 00:08:35.481
and these are just jackal paws
that we found online.

00:08:35.481 --> 00:08:36.815
Let's look at it
real quick again.

00:08:36.815 --> 00:08:38.551
I didn't realize they were
two different ones.

00:08:38.551 --> 00:08:43.656
I guess this is --
that's the front of a jackal,

00:08:43.656 --> 00:08:45.157
and that's a back of the jackal.

00:08:45.157 --> 00:08:46.492
And nobody commented,

00:08:46.492 --> 00:08:49.795
but then this
was the updated one,

00:08:49.795 --> 00:08:53.633
and then someone said, "Hey,
I didn't mind the first time,

00:08:53.633 --> 00:08:55.233
but...

00:08:55.233 --> 00:08:57.436
that wouldn't be how
a jackal would type,

00:08:57.436 --> 00:09:01.406
because that would be
one front paw and one back paw.

00:09:01.406 --> 00:09:03.208
So that would imply that

00:09:03.208 --> 00:09:07.113
the jackal's lying
on its side typing."

00:09:07.113 --> 00:09:08.581
Okay.

00:09:14.654 --> 00:09:15.888
I love that someone's like,

00:09:15.888 --> 00:09:18.390
"I'll go with you on this
for a jackal,

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:19.825
but come on, dude.

00:09:23.795 --> 00:09:26.298
That's stupid."

00:09:26.298 --> 00:09:30.169
I got to confess,
I'm like, ashamed of myself.

00:09:30.169 --> 00:09:35.374
Went day drinking with Lorde --
amazing, so much fun,

00:09:35.374 --> 00:09:37.175
and then we did these paintings.

00:09:37.175 --> 00:09:38.677
We just tried to
recreate the cover

00:09:38.677 --> 00:09:40.479
of one of her albums
in these paintings,

00:09:40.479 --> 00:09:42.681
and then we did, on the
"Late Night" Twitter account,

00:09:42.681 --> 00:09:44.583
basically said,
who painted it better?

00:09:44.583 --> 00:09:46.118
And Lorde won.

00:09:46.118 --> 00:09:49.888
Not like a giant,
but like 53% to 47%.

00:09:49.888 --> 00:09:53.726
And then I'm deeply ashamed,
because then I did a second poll

00:09:53.726 --> 00:09:57.529
on the Sea Captain Polls
Twitter account,

00:09:57.529 --> 00:10:01.099
which I thought would have
less Lorde fans.

00:10:01.099 --> 00:10:05.571
And I phrased it in a way
that I really wanted people

00:10:05.571 --> 00:10:07.806
to vote for me, and I did win,

00:10:07.806 --> 00:10:10.976
but I won by less than Lorde won
in the first vote.

00:10:10.976 --> 00:10:14.179
So I just want to say right now,
Lorde won fair and square

00:10:14.179 --> 00:10:17.415
and I apologize
for trying to rig it.

00:10:17.415 --> 00:10:19.051
I'm ashamed of myself.

00:10:21.887 --> 00:10:27.926
We talked about
honey-baked ham stores

00:10:27.926 --> 00:10:30.695
and how I park across
the street from them,

00:10:30.695 --> 00:10:33.065
because I can't believe
there are people just walking in

00:10:33.065 --> 00:10:35.333
and buying a whole-ass ham.

00:10:35.333 --> 00:10:36.535
A couple of things --

00:10:36.535 --> 00:10:39.171
one, a lot of people defending
honey-baked hams

00:10:39.171 --> 00:10:41.139
being delicious,

00:10:41.139 --> 00:10:43.342
saying I was
out of bounds on that.

00:10:43.342 --> 00:10:49.815
But then someone wrote this
about whole-ass hams.

00:10:49.815 --> 00:10:55.487
"Correction -- technically,
whole-ass ham is redundant,

00:10:55.487 --> 00:10:57.990
because ham comes
from an area of the pig

00:10:57.990 --> 00:11:01.093
that could arguably
be considered its ass,

00:11:01.093 --> 00:11:04.329
and also it would only be
a half-ass ham,

00:11:04.329 --> 00:11:08.667
because it's only one
half of the pig's ass."

00:11:08.667 --> 00:11:10.302
That's poetry.

00:11:13.139 --> 00:11:17.076
Like, I read that
and I was like, this is why.

00:11:17.076 --> 00:11:18.711
This is why we do this.

00:11:21.447 --> 00:11:22.848
Because someday,
you're just gonna be

00:11:22.848 --> 00:11:27.686
scrolling, scrolling through
you know, a YouTube comment,

00:11:27.686 --> 00:11:31.089
and you're gonna read
this beautiful sentence.

00:11:31.089 --> 00:11:32.792
Two sentences.

00:11:36.562 --> 00:11:38.897
Also,

00:11:38.897 --> 00:11:40.232
I feel like we're
pretty committed to

00:11:40.232 --> 00:11:42.535
"Late Night with Seth Meyers,"
but...

00:11:44.503 --> 00:11:48.040
I'd call this show
"half-ass ham."

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:50.609
Alright.

00:11:50.609 --> 00:11:52.378
I think that's about everything.

00:11:53.812 --> 00:11:56.949
And we'll see
you guys next week.

